# ── Generated / derived artifacts (2026-09-22 cleanup) ──────────────────────
# Python bytecode from the vectorbt research spike. Never source, never portable
# across a Python version - the two committed .pyc files were cpython-314.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The "hive" agent-orchestrator's own saved state (agents, tmux targets, pty ids,
# a prompt queue). A different tool's file that happened to sit in this directory
# and got swept in by a bare `git add -A`. Nothing in app/, cli/, setup/,
# scripts/ or tradingview-mcp/ reads it - verified by grep.
roster.json

# Jr kilo (vectorbt regime research) — OUTPUTS, not source. 800 KB of sweep
# results and a 560 KB bar export, all regenerable from the .py files beside
# them via export_bars.py / run_sweep.py. The scripts, the reports and
# requirements.txt stay tracked.
Jr kilo/vectorbt-research/vectorbt_input.csv
Jr kilo/vectorbt-research/sweep_results*.json
Jr kilo/vectorbt-research/regime_sweep_results.json

# cli/cli-paths.json — written by `node cli/discover.js`, and it holds THIS
# machine's absolute paths (C:\Users\Admin\AppData\Local\Programs\PrintingPress\
# bin\...). Committing it means every other clone gets paths that cannot exist.
# Untracked, not deleted: the local file stays and the cli/ scripts keep working.
# Regenerate with: node cli/discover.js
cli/cli-paths.json

# Saved market briefs — one generated JSON per ET date (see cli/README.md).
# Output, not input: market-brief.js --save / gold-brief.js --save write here.
cli/briefs/*.json

# graphify code-analysis tool output (513 KB: graph.html 242 KB, graph.json
# 263 KB, an AST cache and a .sig). Regenerable, machine-specific, and the only
# thing that references it is the graph it generated. app/.graphifyignore stays
# tracked — that one is configuration.
graphify-out/

# One-off analysis artifacts, referenced by nothing in the repo (checked by
# grep over the whole tree):
#  - the 150K eval target ladder: that account is gone, this is a 50K Apex EOD
#    eval now (see app/rules.json firmLimits and Prop Trading/CLAUDE.md).
#  - a single scalping-analysis chart png.
app/MNQ_150K_Eval_Target_Ladder.xlsx
app/week_scalping_analysis.png

# Timestamped backups (app.js.bak-2026-09-17, rules.json.bak-enable-<ts>).
# The blanket `*.bak` above only catches the bare suffix, so this catches the
# dated variants that a restore procedure leaves behind. Ignored, not deleted:
# they are the only copy of a file if a restore was never completed.
*.bak-*
